WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.930
Over a year, a seaside
town keeps two records.

2
00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:07.110
One is how many ice creams
are sold each month.

3
00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:11.110
The other is how many swimming
accidents happen in the sea.

4
00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:15.150
When ice-cream sales go up, the
swimming accidents go up too.

5
00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:18.570
So does eating ice cream make
swimming more dangerous?

6
00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:20.670
Should the town ban ice cream?

7
00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:23.830
In this mission, you'll plot
two sets of data on a scatter

8
00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:24.390
graph.

9
00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:28.190
You'll spot positive,
negative and no correlation.

10
00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:32.570
And you'll ask what a link between
two things can really prove.

11
00:00:32.620 --> 00:00:36.230
Your mission: explain whether
ice cream really causes swimming

12
00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:37.550
accidents.
